# The nightly backup, once a night at 02:30 (D96, D97).
#
# Install it ON THE SERVER, as the user who owns the repository, by opening your
# own crontab and adding the one line below at the end:
#
#     crontab -e
#
# Do NOT run `crontab deploy/backup.cron`: that REPLACES every entry you already
# have, including any job the server already runs. Adding the line by hand is
# the only safe way.
#
# Change /srv/badshahstore below to the folder the repository is checked out in
# on your server; that path is an example, not a fact about your machine.
#
# The whole output goes to the system log through logger, so it appears in
# `journalctl -t badshahstore-backup`. The system log rotates itself (logrotate),
# which is why nothing here writes a log file of its own and why nothing here
# needs cleaning up.
#
# 02:30 is the server's own clock. The retention rule inside the upload counts
# UTC days, so the backup that runs after midnight UTC is the one a "daily"
# backup means.
#
# One line, no continuation:
30 2 * * * cd /srv/badshahstore && /usr/bin/bash deploy/backup.sh 2>&1 | /usr/bin/logger -t badshahstore-backup
